            {
                "entry_id": "f2cf868d-1147-3d7a-9034-be2ac907aaba",
                "word": "archonte",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1dd25fa0-ca2a-4011-9721-13e11ab9606f",
                        "entry_id": "f2cf868d-1147-3d7a-9034-be2ac907aaba",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "archontes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e52c8f4c-57d3-3af3-887b-f06dce976163",
                        "entry_id": "f2cf868d-1147-3d7a-9034-be2ac907aaba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Titre des principaux magistrats dans quelques républiques, et particulièrement à Athènes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Ancient-Greek"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "336a50bc-7627-458f-9395-ca4383229c12",
                                "sense_id": "e52c8f4c-57d3-3af3-887b-f06dce976163",
                                "text": "La puissance des archontes était d’ailleurs considérable : c’était de véritables maîtres de la cité. Ils réunissaient aux pouvoirs administratifs et politiques des pouvoirs judiciaires étendus. Ils étaient pris parmi les plus riches et sortis de charge, ils entraient pour le restant de leur vie dans le grand conseil de l’Aréopage."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d27c2cc0-31a7-47c9-a07f-e5735600bed2",
                        "source_entry_id": "f2cf868d-1147-3d7a-9034-be2ac907aaba",
                        "source_sense_id": "e52c8f4c-57d3-3af3-887b-f06dce976163",
                        "target_lang_word": "archon",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "archon",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8d9aa516-f382-38cb-b8a4-b99a0502fe4a",
                                        "entry_id": "0ef8029c-a0db-36f3-b487-c80d20c7f2ef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A chief magistrate of ancient Athens."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7715cb47-2cf9-4045-a01c-a2579072bcb7",
                                                "sense_id": "8d9aa516-f382-38cb-b8a4-b99a0502fe4a",
                                                "text": "Hated by the archons of Athens for his fearless condemnation of municipal graft, he was hypocritically arraigned on a charge of corrupting Athenian youth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "52054929-26c3-3de7-93ae-12778b417ed4",
                                        "entry_id": "0ef8029c-a0db-36f3-b487-c80d20c7f2ef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who claims the right to rule, or to exercise power or sovereign authority over other human beings."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0c963728-5d3f-3f15-9c6a-a7c666aa0064",
                                        "entry_id": "0ef8029c-a0db-36f3-b487-c80d20c7f2ef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ruler, head of state or other leader."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3179e5e9-4fcd-4952-9cdd-fd58671cb3ae",
                                                "sense_id": "0c963728-5d3f-3f15-9c6a-a7c666aa0064",
                                                "text": "But neither the midwife’s lore nor the caudlectures saved him from the archons of Sinn Fein and their noggin of hemlock."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a503eddb-7435-3eaa-8267-72f741b4dff2",
                                        "entry_id": "0ef8029c-a0db-36f3-b487-c80d20c7f2ef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A supernatural ruler of the cosmos."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c75c6116-343a-4bbb-b0f3-f921a089e72e",
                                                "sense_id": "a503eddb-7435-3eaa-8267-72f741b4dff2",
                                                "text": "Their claim to totality is like the cry of the archon Ialdabaoth that he was the Lord of the Universe and that there was nothing beyond him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a5980210-6598-4a9e-a951-e0f692b625b0",
                        "source_entry_id": "f2cf868d-1147-3d7a-9034-be2ac907aaba",
                        "source_sense_id": "e52c8f4c-57d3-3af3-887b-f06dce976163",
